        "descriptions": [
          {
            "description": "Succisella is a genus of flowering plants in the family Caprifoliaceae. There are four or five species in the genus. They are all native to Europe; three are endemic to the Iberian Peninsula.Amich, F., Devesa, J. A., & Bernardos, S. (2004). Taxonomic revision of the genus Succisella (Dipsacaceae) in the Iberian Peninsula. Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society, 144(3), 351-364. Species include: Succisella andreae-molinae (not accepted by some sources) Succisella carvalhoana Succisella inflexa – southern succisella Succisella microcephala Succisella petteri"
          },
          {
            "description": "Succisella ostensibly means ‘cut off from below’ or ‘abruptly ending’.Gledhill, David (2008). \"The Names of Plants\". Cambridge University Press. (hardback), (paperback). p 366"
          }
